# TriviaBot Game Structure

## Data model

- **Rounds**: 8 rounds + Final Trivia. Each round has `roundType`, `title`, `pointsPerQuestion`, `instructions`, and `questions`.
- **Questions**: `clue`, `answer`, `category`, `isBanned` (client-side). Archive and curated selectors filter with merged banned-question files and used-question ledgers; LLM paths use matching used-ID prefixes as prompt exclusions. Played status belongs to game-list/game-display UI state and does not filter question selection.
- **Round types**: Rounds 1–4, 6, 8 are archive-based; rounds 5 and 7 are LLM (Game Show Style, Mixing Things Up) with subTypes. Use `ROUND_TEMPLATES` in `scripts/generate-game.js` for config.
- **Game list**: `played-status.json` and `data/games/index.json`; games have `isPlayed`. Banned state is in `banned-questions.json` and localStorage.

## Conventions

- One category per round: select 3 questions from the same category per round; shuffle categories and questions (e.g. Fisher–Yates) before selection.
- Shuffle/replace: when regenerating a round (e.g. LLM), mark replaced questions as banned (reason `"shuffled"`) before replacing.
- UI: round color coding R1→R8 is yellow to red; round headers show title, badges, points; format-specific renderers for standard, over/under, list, multiple choice, true/false, Family Feud (top 10 table).

## Key files

- `scripts/generate-game.js` – game generation, `ROUND_TEMPLATES`, selection, LLM rounds, and banned/used-question filtering.
- `js/game-display.js` – render rounds/questions, banned/played UI, shuffle handlers.
- `js/game-list.js` – game list, filters (all/unplayed/played), played status.
- `game.html` – game page; `index.html` – game list.
